  "notes": "The cleared Qualla view establishes ribbed cool-gray corrugated walls and the upper rail-side edge. Transnet documents a brick museum section and public entrance; their position is matched approximately to the mapped east-end entrance. The municipal footprint separates the main 153.56 × 95.379 m shed and small west returns. Three shallow parallel steel roofs are a reconstruction based on span and railway layout; no surveyed roof section was available.",
